    "description": "Rio Grande LNG is a large-scale liquefied natural gas export project under development and construction in Brownsville, Texas. Its customers are global LNG buyers and offtakers seeking long-term liquefaction capacity and LNG supply from the U.S. Gulf Coast. The project is an asset-heavy midstream development whose economics depend on long-term sale and purchase agreements, large-scale project financing, and multiyear construction execution. Public materials state that Phase 1 consists of three liquefaction trains with roughly 18 million tonnes per annum of LNG production capacity and that the broader project is designed for larger total capacity across additional trains. NextDecade announced positive final investment decision on Phase 1 in July 2023 with Global Infrastructure Partners, TotalEnergies, GIC, Mubadala, and other project stakeholders involved in the financing structure. The latest public disclosures reviewed here indicate expected first LNG from Phase 1 in 2027, but they do not fully disclose the current project-company ownership breakdown across all investors.",
